  "findings": [
    "The collapse is defined from actual exhaustive old/new labels, with the new label sent to j and every old label proved to recover its unique parent. Classical.choose is constrained by the proven old-label injectivity, not an assumed root-word correspondence.",
    "All distinct ordered triples avoiding simultaneous membership of old(j) and new(j) are covered. Exhaustion places the new label in any of the three slots; swap/cyclic identities transport its sign with the exact orientation. The all-old branch is an exact identity. Admissibility is not needed for these nonexceptional parent-limit triples beyond parent G1.",
    "Finite eventually_all over all three child label indices obtains one neighborhood. Degenerate or forbidden triples are implication cases, not additional caller restrictions on the allowed triples. The positive-radius theorem intersects this with the already source-derived child G1 radius.",
    "The exceptional value is exactly -sign(det q (P k-P j)). For every k!=j, admissibility gives its nonzero determinant. The two chi identities read (B,A,X) and (X,B,A), precisely the reversed increasing far-triple orientations; the second is a cyclic permutation of the first.",
    "The cyclic predecessor and successor exceptional values equal attachmentMinus/Plus via exact attachment identities at the harmless positive parameter1. They do not assume that the child at1 is G1 or lies on the small interval.",
    "The final package assumes only hn3, parent G1 and SoftAdmissible. It concludes child G1 on one positive radius and the full ordered-triple data. It never asserts Generic/G1 at zero, and it does not supply the still-needed boundary-word/root correspondence.",
    "Root observed terminal exit0 for first kernel52951; 10 standard-only traces and 9 full-body embeddings are receipt-bound. First drafts are unchanged."
  ],
